{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "The Big Argument", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Oh, I Wish ...", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 11, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 1, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Exchange information about people's interests and backgrounds using a wider range of language.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "engenn8le01ob11re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Managing a Conversation", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "It is common to show you understand someone's feelings in a conversation. <br/>You use negative questions to confirm information you already know.<br/>You use <span class=\"italic\">\u201cI wish ...\u201d</span> to talk about things you do not have or do, or you cannot have or do.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Negative questions can have two different meanings. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can ask a negative question for confirmation of a positive belief. <br/>You can ask a negative question for confirmation of a negative belief.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example: <br/><span class=\"italic\">Don't you think I wish things were different for me?</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The verb <span class=\"italic\">wish</span> introduces an idea. After <span class=\"italic\">wish</span>, you use a verb in the past tense.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I wish I knew ...<br/>I wish I had ...<br/>I wish you were \u2026", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Structure: <br/>Wish + Simple Past tense<br/><br/>Example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">I wish it wasn't always the case.<br>I wish I had asked her out in college.", "type": "text"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Modals For Possibility, Certainty, Suggestions and Expectations", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use modals when you want to express possibility, certainty, suggestions and expectations.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">You use may, might and could to express possibility in the past and in the future.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "*Might suggests that something is less possible that may", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ul><li>might / might not + infinitive</li><li>could / could not + infinitive</li><li>may / may not + infinitive</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example: ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">She even said that he might be her soulmate.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<br/><span class=\"strong\">Expressing Certainty</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use must to express that something is necessarily true.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">The girl of your dreams must be in a comic book store!</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Should, could, might and would are used to express suggestions:</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example: <br/><span class=\"italic\">You should keep your eyes open this time.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<br/>You can also use <span class=\"strong\">supposed to</span> to express expectation.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example: <br/><span class=\"italic\">I know what you're supposed to do.</span>", "type": "text"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "miserable", "type": "name"}, {"content": "terrible, awful ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It made my mother feel miserable. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le01ob11aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words to review.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "gutsy", "type": "name"}, {"content": "showing courage and determination", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Going to Italy to meet her boyfriend was very gutsy.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le01ob11aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "soulmate", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person with whom someone has a deep affinity; life companion", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Don't you think it's wonderful to have a soulmate?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le01ob11aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to have a crush", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be infatuated with someone", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Sally told me that Camilla has a crush on me.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le01ob11aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "obvious", "type": "name"}, {"content": "predictable and easily understood", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I only found out she had a crush on me after Sally pointed out that it was pretty obvious.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le01ob11aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "nerd", "type": "name"}, {"content": "someone obsessively interested in a particular subject ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  I'm a comic book nerd. Not all my dates understand that.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le01ob11aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "slow on the uptake", "type": "name"}, {"content": "slow to understand something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: <span class=\"strong\">Mike</span>: You've always been slow on the uptake when it comes to girls, Peter.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le01ob11aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "sensible", "type": "name"}, {"content": "reasonable and wise", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: <span class=\"strong\">Ann</span>: I should hire an assistant manager. <span class=\"strong\">Bob</span>: That sounds like a sensible idea.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le01ob11aud08", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "spontaneous", "type": "name"}, {"content": "natural and genuine", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: If I call Camilla, I won't sound spontaneous.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le01ob11aud09", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Brainstorm some common regrets people may have with a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use negative questions to confirm understanding.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make sentences using <span class=\"italic\">wish</span> to talk about common regrets.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make sentences about 5 of your own regrets about dating.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use <span class=\"italic\">wish</span> to introduce the ideas.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use <span class=\"italic\">should have</span> and <span class=\"italic\">supposed to</span> for adding details.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I express possibility, certainty, suggestions and expectations.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I encourage agreement and show I understand someone's feelings or situation. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I reflect on relationships.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "contents": [{}], "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "engenn8le01ob11re2img05.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn8le01ob11re2img05.jpg", "time": "100", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>:\t\tPeter! You look miserable! What happened?<br/><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>:\t\tI finally gave Camilla a call. <br/><span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>:\t\tWow! That was a gutsy move. <br><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>:\t\tShe told me she already had a boyfriend. She's been with him for a couple of months already. She even said that he might be her soulmate.<br/><span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>:\t\tAw, I'm sorry, Peter. That must've felt like a shock."}, {"image": "engenn8le01ob11re2img01.jpg", "time": "20200", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>:\t\tI wish I wasn't so slow on the uptake! I should've realized she had a crush on me back in college!<br/><span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>:\t\tYou just take a while to understand what's going on sometimes, that's all.<br/><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>:\t\tThings don't always seem obvious to me, you know that! I wish it wasn't always the case.<br/><span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>:\t\tI think you've always been more interested in your comics than real-life situations, perhaps. Don't you wish you were more grounded in reality?"}, {"image": "engenn8le01ob11re2img05.jpg", "time": "41800", "id": 3, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>:\t\tSally, I'm a nerd. I've tried sounding like a more sensible kind of guy, but it has always failed to impress anyone. No matter how hard I try, I can never sound spontaneous when I'm out of my element. Don't you think I wish things were different for me?<br/><span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>:\t\tIn that case, I know what you're supposed to do. The girl of your dreams must be in a comic book store. You should keep your eyes open this time!"}], "audiosrc": "engenn8le01ob11re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn8le01ob11re2img05.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": " I can talk about what I do, did or have done.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can express possibility, certainty, suggestions and expectations.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can encourage agreement and show I understand someone's feelings or situation. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " Do you have a friend who has had bad luck with dating?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " If you could give 3 pieces of advice about dating to a friend, what would they be? ", "type": "Free Header Item"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "Let's review!", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "id": 0, "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0]}, {"template_override": 1, "questions": [{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "type": "question"}], "id": 0, "responses": [{"correct": 0, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "id": 0}, {"correct": 1, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "id": 1}]}], "type": "STI", "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": " Sadly, in love, as in everything else, when <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_0\">you snooze, you lose</span>!", "type": "text"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Content", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct!", "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something import